var help_default = "Usage: akm-migrate <command> [options]\n\nThe one migration tool for an akm installation. The CLI proper reads every\nshape akm has ever written (in memory, with a warning); `apply` makes the\ncurrent shape durable on disk. `status` and `apply` run every step, in\norder, and print one combined JSON plan (exit 1 when any step is blocked):\n\n  1. config.json rewritten in its current shape (unknown keys dropped, the\n     `engines`/`defaults` form converted to `connections`/`harnesses` with\n     `defaults.improveStrategy` as `improve.strategy`, `configVersion` set\n     to the current value) -- backed up first. A config in the pre-0.9.15\n     source layout is refused, not converted: run this under akm 0.9.x. Keys akm no longer reads from config (an engine's\n     `apiKeyFile`, a literal or `${secrets/...}` `apiKey`, and the same on a\n     connection or `embedding`) move to\n     credentials.json, one note per key (never its value); a key that cannot\n     be moved stays on the connection as `apiKey`, with a note. The retired\n     models.json is folded into the models of the connections and harnesses\n     it names (the entries it cannot place are listed in the notes), then\n     moved to the config backups. A connection or harness akm cannot use stays in the\n     file as written, with a note on what to fix\n  2. pending state.db migrations, historical-destructive ones included,\n     with a verified sibling safety copy (the only path that admits them)\n  3. task files at version 2 or 3, and version 4 files still carrying the\n     retired `schedule[].enabled` key, rewritten as task source v4 under\n     one backup directory per run\n  4. the retired `engine:` key on commands, agents, workflows and task\n     sources rewritten to `connection:` or `harness:` by what the name is\n     now, under one backup directory per run\n  5. refs in the text files akm indexes in writable bundles that still use\n     the spelling from before refs became bundle paths (`knowledge/WORK/x`,\n     now `WORK/x`), in frontmatter and body: `[bundle//]<folder>/<path>`,\n     `<type>:<path>` and `wiki:<path>`, rewritten under one backup directory\n     per run. An old spelling that is now another file's ref is not\n     rewritten, only listed\n  6. superseded residue removed: pre-0.9.0 `.akm` leftovers in the stash,\n     and the transaction-journal, maintenance-barrier, lock-mutex and\n     version-stamp files older releases kept under $DATA, $STATE and $CONFIG\n\n`akm migrate status|apply` wraps this executable; `akm upgrade` runs\n`apply` after its install step, so an image that ships akm can put either\nin its entrypoint (a current installation is a no-op).\n\nCommands:\n  status               Inspect every pending migration without changing anything.\n  apply [--dry-run]    Back up and apply every pending migration.\n";

